------------------------------------
# Create simple .yaml file


apiVersion:  # Kubernetes API version used to manage the resource.
kind:        # Type of resource: Pod, Deployment, Service, Node, etc.
metadata:    # Information identifying the resource. Dictionary.
spec:        # Desired state and configuration of the resource. Dictionary.
spec > containers  # Define the containers . List of dictionaries

# yaml file code here
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod

metadata:
  name: nginx-pod

spec:
  containers:                      
    - name: nginx-container
      image: nginx


To run use:
$ kubectl apply -f fileName.yaml                  
      # apply -> Make this resource match my declared configuration.
      # create -> Create this resource.


Other commands:
$ kubectl run hello-world
$ kubectl cluster-info
$ kubectl get nodes 


$ kubectl get pods 
$ kubectl get pods -A
$ kubectl describe pod podNameHere          # In-depth information about the pod. 

$ kubectl exec -it POD -- sh       

$ kubectl get nodes -o wide         # information with “node”. 



kubectl get pods -o wide
kubectl get nodes -o wide
kubectl get deployments -o wide
kubectl get services -o wide



# Delete: a resource. 
$ kubectl delete pod nginx1
$ kubectl delete node worker1


# Edit the Pod:
$ kubectl edit pod podName











